{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "P11049", "secondaryAccessions": ["B4DVC1", "Q3KPF9"], "uniProtkbId": "CD37_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1989-07-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1990-11-01", "entryVersion": 197, "sequenceVersion": 2}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Leukocyte antigen CD37"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Tetraspanin-26"}, "shortNames": [{"value": "Tspan-26"}]}], "cdAntigenNames": [{"value": "CD37"}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "CD37"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "TSPAN26"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q61451"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17182550"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "22624718"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26784544"}], "value": "Structural component of specialized membrane microdomains known as tetraspanin-enriched microdomains (TERMs), which act as platforms for receptor clustering and signaling. Participates thereby in diverse biological functions such as cell signal transduction, adhesion, migration and protein trafficking (PubMed:22624718). Upon ligand binding, two signaling pathways are activated, one acting through phosphorylation by LYN leading to cell death or a survival pathway with activation of GSK3B (PubMed:22624718). Plays an essential role essential for clustering of integrin ITGA4/ITGB1 and promotes its mobility in the plasma membrane of B-cells. In turn, participates in ITGA4/ITGB1 integrin-mediated antiapoptotic signaling through AKT (By similarity). Also plays a role in the migration of dendritic cells and neutrophils to draining lymph nodes, as well as in their integrin-mediated adhesion (By similarity). Negatively regulates IL-6 responses through direct interaction with SOCS3 thereby preventing constitutive IL-6 signaling (PubMed:26784544). Alternatively, inhibition of IL-6 signaling can also occur via interaction and stabilization of DECTIN1/CLEC7A at the cell membrane to inhibit its ability to promote the production of IL-6 (PubMed:17182550)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17182550"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21930792"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26784544"}], "value": "Interacts with SCIMP (PubMed:21930792). Interacts with SOCS3 (PubMed:26784544). Interacts with DECTIN1/CLEC7A (PubMed:17182550)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P11049", "intActId": "EBI-6139068"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P19397", "geneName": "CD53", "intActId": "EBI-6657396"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P11049", "intActId": "EBI-6139068"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P54849", "geneName": "EMP1", "intActId": "EBI-4319440"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P11049", "intActId": "EBI-6139068"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P08034", "geneName": "GJB1", "intActId": "EBI-17565645"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P11049", "intActId": "EBI-6139068"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q8TAF8", "geneName": "LHFPL5", "intActId": "EBI-2820517"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDi